    2441	**Statement.** Let `f_N(z) := Σ_{n=2}^{N} χ_P(n) z^n` (length N+1, weight
    2442	M = π(N)). For every rational `a/q` with `(a, q) = 1` and `q ≤ Q`,
    2443	
    2444	  `R(a/q; primes) := |f_N(e^{2π i a/q})| / √π(N)
    2445	                   = √π(N) · μ(q)² / φ(q) + O(√(2 log N))`
    2446	
    2447	verified empirically at `N ∈ {2^{10}, 2^{12}, 2^{14}, 2^{16}, 2^{18}}`
    2448	for `1 ≤ q ≤ 58` (limited only by FFT resolution at small N). The
    2449	fluctuation `O(√(2 log N))` is Salem-Zygmund / Vinogradov-typical noise.
    2450	
    2451	**Consequence.** `‖f_N‖_∞ = (1 + o(1)) · √π(N) = (1 + o(1)) · M^{1/2}`,
    2452	attained at `z = e^{i π} = −1` (the q=2 parity major arc). Equivalently:
    2453	`R_N := ‖f_N‖_∞ / √π(N) → 1` (because the dominant rational point
    2454	contributes √π(N) · μ²(2)/φ(2) = √π(N)).
