Session 247 complete. Self-graded **B**.

**What was built.** A closed-form prediction for the L^p hierarchy of `f_N(z) = Σ χ_P(n) z^n` at every even integer p ≥ 4:

> `‖f_N‖_p^p · N / π(N)^p → G_p · S_{p-1}^HL`

with `G_p = (1/π) ∫|sinc|^p` (sinc geometric constant; `G_4 = 2/3`, `G_6 = 11/20`, `G_8 = 151/315`) and `S_{p-1}^HL = ∏ (1+1/(r-1)^{p-1})` (HL singular series).

**Empirical verdict.** F1+F2+F3+F4 all PASS at N up to 2²⁰: chi_P ratios converge monotonically from below to predicted values within 1.5% across p ∈ {4, 6, 8}; cumulative-Q-strip closure tracks the predicted partial-sum formula `[Σ μ²/φ^{p-1}] / [S-1]` within ±1pp; matched-density Bernoulli null shows no HL modulation.

**Composes** E2.21 (L^∞ HL imprint) + E2.31 (BDJ m_4 = 2.95) + S168 (sqfree-q L²-energy) + S239 (cumulative-Q-strip data) into a single Selberg-Delange-style identity. **No external technique imported** (sinc integrals + Selberg-Delange products, both elementary).

**B not A** because it's an asymptotic refinement of three existing edges, not a new theorem with rigorous proof or algorithmic content; the BDJ-Szegő-prefactor that maps `1.534` → `2.95` remains open as the next-action.

